// `later<R>(text): Promise<R>` resolves to parsed data, and R is only what the caller claims. Two such promises go through Promise.all, and the first result is a tagged union. The program must behave as in plain Bun.
type Part = { id?: number; name?: string; more?: unknown }
class Unrelated { k = 1; j = 2; e = 3; ok = 4; value = 5; data = 6; error = 7; held = 8 }
